# =====================================================================
# puller — .dockerignore  (DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH; INERT TODAY)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS: This repo has NO Dockerfile and is NOT containerized. Its
# ~40 jobs run as GitHub Actions cron steps, so a .dockerignore is a
# NO-OP right now (there is no `docker build` to feed it).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS ANYWAY:
# If puller ever grows a Dockerfile (e.g. `COPY . .`), this file is the
# guard that keeps local secrets, venvs, git metadata, and multi-GB
# spacy/model blobs OUT of the pushed image layer. Cheap to add now,
# prevents a whole class of "oops we shipped .env in the image" leaks
# later.
#
# NOTE: We do NOT blanket-ignore "*.yaml" so that if a future
# image DOES need a config yaml, it can still be COPYed; the specific
# secret-file patterns below cover the real risk.
# =====================================================================

# ---- version control -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ---- secrets & credentials ------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.*
*secret*.json
*secret*.yaml
*secret*.yml
*-secrets.yaml
*-secrets.yml
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.b64

# ---- python build / cache -------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyi
venv/
.venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---- large ML / spacy blobs -----------------------------------------
*.nlp
*.spacy
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.vec
models/
spacy_models/

# ---- os / editor noise ----------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
*.tmp
node_modules/
